---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import EnquiryPanel from '../components/EnquiryPanel.astro';
import { property } from '../data/property';

const waNumber = (property.contact.phone ?? '').replace(/[^0-9]/g, '');
const whatsapp = `https://wa.me/${waNumber}?text=${encodeURIComponent('Olá Luisa, we would like to ask about two families buying Quinta Fonte do Palheiro together.')}`;
---

<Layout
  title="Co-buying guide: two families, one estate | Quinta Fonte do Palheiro"
  description="How two families could share Quinta Fonte do Palheiro near Salir, Loulé: €890,000 asking, €445,000 per family, and the questions to ask a Portuguese lawyer about compropriedade or a company structure."
>
  <SiteHeader ctaHref="#enquire" />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="guide-hero">
      <div class="guide-hero__inner">
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Co-buying guide · family estate</p>
        <h1>Two families,<br /><em>one estate.</em></h1>
        <p class="guide-hero__lede">Quinta Fonte do Palheiro has two independent, furnished houses on 2.5 ha. That makes a shared purchase more practical than the usual “one villa, one family” search. This guide sets out the arithmetic and the questions to take to a lawyer. It is not legal or tax advice.</p>
        <a class="button button--ochre" data-event="Co-buy click" data-label="Guide – WhatsApp" href={whatsapp} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ask us about co-buying <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" aria-label="The arithmetic">
      <p class="eyebrow">The arithmetic</p>
      <div class="guide-section__body">
        <h2>€890,000 between<br /><em>two families.</em></h2>
        <div class="math-card">
          <div><span>Asking price</span><strong>€890,000</strong></div>
          <span class="math-card__operator" aria-hidden="true">÷ 2</span>
          <div><span>Per family</span><strong>€445,000</strong></div>
        </div>
        <p>€445,000 each is less than a standard Algarve villa costs per family — and the estate comes with a second house, a saltwater pool, own water, 3-phase power and an 11 kW EV charger. The split is arithmetic, not a quote: legal fees, tax, financing, insurance and running costs are on top, and each family should take its own advice on those.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section guide-section--sand" aria-label="Ownership structures">
      <p class="eyebrow">Two structures to discuss</p>
      <div class="guide-section__body">
        <h2>How you hold it<br /><em>matters.</em></h2>
        <div class="guide-grid">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Compropriedade</h3>
            <p>Joint ownership of the same property, with shares recorded in the deed. Ask a Portuguese lawyer how shares are transferred, how decisions are made, and what happens if one family wants to sell or stops paying its share of costs.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>A company structure</h3>
            <p>A company holds the property and the families hold shares. Ask about setup and ongoing costs, mortgage and tax treatment, who can live in which house, and the process for a shareholder leaving.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="guide-note">Both routes need professional setup. Neither should be chosen from a webpage. Confirm the details with a Portuguese property lawyer and an independent tax adviser before you commit.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-section" aria-label="Checklist">
      <p class="eyebrow">First meeting with the lawyer</p>
      <div class="guide-section__body">
        <h2>Nine questions,<br /><em>asked early.</em></h2>
        <ol class="guide-list">
          <li>Which house does each family occupy, and is that written into the agreement?</li>
          <li>How are purchase, legal and tax costs divided?</li>
          <li>How are maintenance, utilities and insurance shared month to month?</li>
          <li>What happens if one family wants to sell its share?</li>
          <li>What happens on death, incapacity or a family moving home?</li>
          <li>Can either family let its house, and under what rules?</li>
          <li>How are decisions about the shared pool, bar and workshop made?</li>
          <li>What does each structure mean for mortgage approval and tax each year?</li>
          <li>What does due diligence show for each building and the water rights?</li>
        </ol>
        <p><a class="guide-inline-link" data-event="FAQ click" data-label="Buyer facts from co-buying guide" href="/buyer-facts?utm_source=site&utm_medium=cta&utm_campaign=family-pivot">Read the buyer facts before that meeting <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-cta">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Next step</p>
      <h2>See both houses<br /><em>on a live video call.</em></h2>
      <p>We will walk the main house and the second house separately, so each family can picture its own front door. Then you take the questions above to your lawyer.</p>
      <div class="guide-cta__links">
        <a class="button button--paper" data-event="Walkthrough click" data-label="Co-buying guide CTA" href={whatsapp} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a video walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="guide-inline-link guide-inline-link--light" data-event="Co-buy click" data-label="Back to estate" href="/?utm_source=site&utm_medium=cta&utm_campaign=family-pivot">Back to the estate <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <EnquiryPanel interest="two families buying together" />
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>

<style>
  .guide-hero { min-height: min(38rem, 78svh); display: flex; align-items: end; padding: 9rem var(--page-edge) 4rem; color: var(--paper); background: var(--ink) url('/images/areal1.jpg') center 56% / cover no-repeat; position: relative; isolation: isolate; }
  .guide-hero::before { content: ''; position: absolute; z-index: -1; inset: 0; background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(8,28,21,.9), rgba(8,28,21,.48) 60%, rgba(8,28,21,.12)); }
  .guide-hero__inner { max-width: 44rem; }
  .guide-hero h1 { margin: 1rem 0 1.4rem; font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 6.6vw, 7rem); line-height: .9; letter-spacing: -.018em; font-weight: 400; }
  .guide-hero h1 em { color: var(--ochre); font-weight: 400; }
  .guide-hero__lede { max-width: 36rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; color: rgba(246,242,231,.86); line-height: 1.65; }
  .guide-section { padding: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 9rem) var(--page-edge); display: grid; grid-template-columns: .6fr 1.4fr; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 6rem); }
  .guide-section--sand { background: var(--sand); }
  .guide-section__body { max-width: 46rem; }
  .guide-section h2 { margin-bottom: 1.7rem; font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 4.2vw, 4.6rem); line-height: .94; letter-spacing: -.015em; font-weight: 400; }
  .guide-section h2 em { color: var(--clay); font-weight: 400; }
  .guide-section p { color: rgba(23,54,45,.8); line-height: 1.7; }
  .math-card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; margin: 0 0 1.7rem; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: .3rem; background: rgba(238,231,220,.5); }
  .math-card div span, .math-card div strong { display: block; }
  .math-card div span { font: 500 .58rem/1.3 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(23,54,45,.66); }
  .math-card div strong { margin-top: .35rem; font: 400 clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3.2rem)/1 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  .math-card__operator { font: 400 1.4rem/1 var(--font-display); color: var(--clay); }
  .guide-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.7rem; }
  .guide-grid article { border-top: 2px solid var(--clay); padding: 1.2rem 1.2rem 1.35rem; background: rgba(252,250,246,.5); border-radius: 0 0 .25rem .25rem; }
  .guide-grid article > span { font: 500 .6rem/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .1em; color: var(--clay); }
  .guide-grid h3 { margin: .7rem 0 .6rem; font-size: 1.9rem; line-height: 1; }
  .guide-grid p { font-size: .97rem; }
  .guide-note { padding-top: 1.2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: .9rem; }
  .guide-list { list-style: none; counter-reset: q; margin-bottom: 1.7rem; }
  .guide-list li { counter-increment: q; padding: 1rem 0 1rem 3.2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); position: relative; color: rgba(23,54,45,.82); }
  .guide-list li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .guide-list li::before { content: counter(q, decimal-leading-zero); position: absolute; left: 0; top: 1.05rem; color: var(--clay); font: 500 .65rem/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .guide-inline-link { color: var(--clay); font: 500 .65rem/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--clay); padding-bottom: .25rem; }
  .guide-inline-link:hover { color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); }
  .guide-inline-link--light { color: var(--ochre); border-color: var(--ochre); }
  .guide-inline-link--light:hover { color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--paper); }
  .guide-cta { padding: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem) var(--page-edge); background: var(--clay); color: var(--paper); }
  .guide-cta h2 { margin: 1rem 0 1.4rem; font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 4.6vw, 5rem); line-height: .92; letter-spacing: -.015em; font-weight: 400; }
  .guide-cta h2 em { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 400; }
  .guide-cta p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 36rem; color: rgba(246,242,231,.88); }
  .guide-cta__links { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem 2rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .guide-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .guide-hero { min-height: 36rem; padding-top: 8rem; } .guide-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .math-card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; text-align: center; } .math-card__operator { display: none; } }
</style>
